                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "cada9d12-5915-41bc-aa50-1038100b4316",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "tags": [
                            "present",
                            "singular",
                            "third-person"
                        ],
                        "form": "overflushes"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "15d540a4-fb65-4b40-b18b-175507968d0d",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "overflushing"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "098af81e-98e1-4bb8-b167-b2e7584b69b0",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "overflushed"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "a63ce4d1-be1c-433b-ae3a-b991d767d685",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "overflushed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a71675ef-c0f7-3dea-b1ae-28fe0d32b6ee",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To flush to excess.",
                            "To flood with too much liquid while cleansing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "32d896a8-59f2-459f-8dfd-c4045e5f1f05",
                                "sense_id": "a71675ef-c0f7-3dea-b1ae-28fe0d32b6ee",
                                "text": "It is a bad plan to overflush ewes, as they usually suffer more from loss of flesh during winter. The best plan is to get them fleshy, and then keep them thriving whilst with the ram."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc539279-1f43-4e0f-b4b7-167dd7bce3c5",
                                "sense_id": "a71675ef-c0f7-3dea-b1ae-28fe0d32b6ee",
                                "text": "It is possible to overflush the casing and render it difficult to use. Too much soaking or flushing, or the use of water that is too hot, will remove some of the natural oils from the casings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "08c5b64b-ca73-4d5b-b8d0-b757b4276f2b",
                                "sense_id": "a71675ef-c0f7-3dea-b1ae-28fe0d32b6ee",
                                "text": "As part of the clean-up operations which took place on November 1, they were found guilty of having overflushed the scene of the accident during clearance work, which caused additional pollution of the Rhine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99a27e7a-f3e1-4417-974d-ba8fa449b48d",
                                "sense_id": "a71675ef-c0f7-3dea-b1ae-28fe0d32b6ee",
                                "text": "Catheter care includes flushing with 0.2-0.4 mL sterile heparinized saline every 6-8 hours if an infusion is not being administered through the needle. It is important not to overflush the system in small animals, causing systemic heparinization."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f8c4e237-2f2c-30ad-ae30-d910f9b7c40c",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To flush to excess.",
                            "To flush too many toilets."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb7038cb-c660-4fd0-be7a-9cc21a060d36",
                                "sense_id": "f8c4e237-2f2c-30ad-ae30-d910f9b7c40c",
                                "text": "No substance goes out from you by perspiration, except the noxious matter that you ought to get rid of; and you might as well ask if the dinners of a city might not be diminished were its sewers overflushed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7425cc01-6e6d-4198-8c99-1022796e7d62",
                                "sense_id": "f8c4e237-2f2c-30ad-ae30-d910f9b7c40c",
                                "text": "Again, children are more exposed to sewer-poisoning because they are kept indoors during \"bad weather,\" just when the gases are rising into the house from the overflushed sewers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8eb28447-6b57-4ca9-ba15-91b3f1e2b45e",
                                "sense_id": "f8c4e237-2f2c-30ad-ae30-d910f9b7c40c",
                                "text": "It is possible to overflush, and so injure the sewers."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb2f5594-3557-390a-89a3-62fbbb035334",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To flush to excess.",
                            "To flood or inundate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "48b3195d-7a94-4455-a6ed-99f07eeb016e",
                                "sense_id": "eb2f5594-3557-390a-89a3-62fbbb035334",
                                "text": "But Men when overflush'd with Drink, Are feldom capable to think."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32c7c3d8-fe74-451b-acf0-c789934c3eaa",
                                "sense_id": "eb2f5594-3557-390a-89a3-62fbbb035334",
                                "text": "I've seen that fiend-law's introduction, In spite of Fielden, Stanhope , Oastler and the good: – Its mildest aim, murder and seduction, To overflush our streets with agony and blood!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09c49642-914a-4432-ab84-b445d296c1a7",
                                "sense_id": "eb2f5594-3557-390a-89a3-62fbbb035334",
                                "text": "The protesting sects have pulled Him out of the shrine, smashing it in violent bitterness of hatred: they have overflushed Him with lusty blood, made Him hail-fellow walking amongst men, and they have brought Him into intimate hobnobbery with the multitude;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b277eb0-7aa6-4eef-95e3-5a0a752e9f5b",
                                "sense_id": "eb2f5594-3557-390a-89a3-62fbbb035334",
                                "text": "But my interest in it is that I do not want to see the Commodity Credit Corporation flushing into an already overflushed market additional oil which only serves to help certain of the secondary processing companies, such as some of the large, oh, the companies that make this syntetic lard, what have you -- [laughter] you know, the vegetable oil."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "984d43f4-0eba-39c1-8bb0-4c77e8527162",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To flush over.",
                            "To cover with or suffuse with a tinge or glow of color."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8b37339-d5a4-4996-a127-a0ad2573a697",
                                "sense_id": "984d43f4-0eba-39c1-8bb0-4c77e8527162",
                                "text": "[…] still they have a fragrance of nature about them, and a freshness, such as Scottish noses snuff up from bleak moors and green fields, envying not at all the strong aroma that flows from exuberant fields overflushed with the living gold and purple of a rich tropical vegetation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bfcdd38a-5270-49c2-a257-7072eb547150",
                                "sense_id": "984d43f4-0eba-39c1-8bb0-4c77e8527162",
                                "text": "A listening, longing silence fell Upon the elm-trees like a spell Of expectation and desire, And quick I saw the impulsive fire Of sunset overflush the white And waiting clouds with rosy light;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f788a7d-3e52-41aa-a2cc-734bb360cf5d",
                                "sense_id": "984d43f4-0eba-39c1-8bb0-4c77e8527162",
                                "text": "I went down on the wide beach, where nobody was, because the stretches of sand are wet and chalky, and the rocks are rough and pooly -- only three shrimpers waded along the wonderful outspreading ruffling water, pushing their great nets before them, stopping, picking out the little objects, and moving on again through the marvellous green light overflushed with ruddy gleams."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "795179c7-8090-3fc2-b7d8-25cca35c08b3",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To flush over.",
                            "To cover the face with blushing or a flush."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "84c40169-a61f-4911-be92-aea2793668e2",
                                "sense_id": "795179c7-8090-3fc2-b7d8-25cca35c08b3",
                                "text": "When Bernard de Avelyne concluded his ballad of Chivalry, the brightness that overflushed his face became gradually darker, his palsied hands forsook the harp, he buried his face in his hands and his hoary hair, and seemed to labour under that bodily as well as mental depression which sometimes succeeds sudden unwonted exertion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f1dadd0-5410-4530-ba2b-d52c2d19971c",
                                "sense_id": "795179c7-8090-3fc2-b7d8-25cca35c08b3",
                                "text": "When first perceived Is there no sweet strife to forget, to change, To overflush those blemishes with all The glow of general goodness they disturb ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f943bb7-d5b1-4254-95ca-0a80309f3901",
                                "sense_id": "795179c7-8090-3fc2-b7d8-25cca35c08b3",
                                "text": "It does not defy death and futurity, for a doubt of its kingship over them never overflushed the majestic havir of its serene countenance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed2229b3-3b57-4e01-9aed-e5fc81a878f2",
                                "sense_id": "795179c7-8090-3fc2-b7d8-25cca35c08b3",
                                "text": "But look, they change, they seem to overflush."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "89d3265a-2104-3e59-a18f-72a0f25119f2",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To flush over.",
                            "To suffuse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "199227f8-51f5-4b87-9c73-5265b1d1b363",
                                "sense_id": "89d3265a-2104-3e59-a18f-72a0f25119f2",
                                "text": "Men, it is true, have probably far exceeded them in the actual amount of verse overflushed with feeling which they have created."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1651d469-5717-4497-a28e-6e213bd1f6b6",
                                "sense_id": "89d3265a-2104-3e59-a18f-72a0f25119f2",
                                "text": "Religion has evanished from this late Renaissance art, nor has the afterglow of Guido Reni's hectic piety yet overflushed it."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bcbf665a-684f-3a53-bb5f-dfb457ce34f5",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To flush over.",
                            "To wash over."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3ce0ecc-dd35-4c44-9043-c89a007f661d",
                                "sense_id": "bcbf665a-684f-3a53-bb5f-dfb457ce34f5",
                                "text": "As Eloquence vpon a trotting nagge Out-ambles Wisdom in a morris daunce, Or as the waves doe overflush the crag — Gie rocks of fortune on the shores of Fraunce;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9474f808-01c0-486f-aa36-432d61985155",
                                "sense_id": "bcbf665a-684f-3a53-bb5f-dfb457ce34f5",
                                "text": "The acute, infectious cold, which is the basis of much later infection, could be rendered a far less potent cause of disorganization if all schoolrooms were overflushed with open air night and day."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db32967c-4359-3fd4-b101-6ce4987fe821",
                        "entry_id": "137c4c02-819d-3fa1-a9f2-e539d4874c8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To force overflush into a system in order to clear out the active fluids."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0d635b9-724e-4e79-b532-25e8e86e700a",
                                "sense_id": "db32967c-4359-3fd4-b101-6ce4987fe821",
                                "text": "Overflush with 150 barrels of water ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ef59de2-b653-4ab4-9cdd-69f9f877678a",
                                "sense_id": "db32967c-4359-3fd4-b101-6ce4987fe821",
                                "text": "The larger volume of crude was pumped in an attempt to overflush the fracture as effectively as possible."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3cf87656-bc0b-46bb-a64c-1e5b4dd27c5c",
                                "sense_id": "db32967c-4359-3fd4-b101-6ce4987fe821",
                                "text": "But it is still recommended not to overflush in horizontal wells as there could be loss in near wellbore conductivity."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
